[Music]  the marvel cinematic universe has  clearly experienced  massive success however that doesn't  mean the studio's  sprawling saga is devoid of missteps  from unfortunate casting decisions  to creative control issues here are some  of the regrets that the people behind  the franchise  have had about the universe they helped  create  thor the dark world has not enjoyed the  best reputation among  mcu movies not only did it get the worst  reviews of any feature in the franchise  but even its own director alan taylor  has publicly expressed disappointment  over how the project turned out  specifically taylor has been pretty open  about how he didn't end up having as  much of a creative impact on the  production  as he wanted the first inkling of taylor  having a difficult experience on the  project came up as early as  october 2013 when the director while  promoting the theatrical release of the  dark world  revealed that he and marvel studios had  disagreements over how to deliver  exposition throughout the movie  taylor would get more explicit in later  interviews coming right out and saying  that the final cut of the movie was  different from what he initially wanted  taylor explained to uproxx the marvel  experience  was particularly wrenching because i was  sort of given absolute  freedom while we were shooting and then  in post it turned into a different movie  so that is something i hope never to  repeat and don't wish upon  anybody else based on that quote it  sounds like taylor definitely won't be  directing any marvel movies in the near  future  unless of course he has a serious heart  to heart with executives at the studio  i wish i could trust you it took a few  mcu appearances for the franchise to  really get the god of thunder right  thor ragnarok solidified what this  character was all about but before then  thor was on shakier ground the character  was a little more traditional in his  initial outings  and he lacked the consistently engaging  and subversive personalities that his  fellow avengers received  one of several ways thor's earlier  appearances came up short was in a tiny  detail from the first thor movie  one related to chris hemsworth's  eyebrows yes  his eyebrows this revelation came  directly from the president of marvel  studios  mr kevin feige himself he said that if  he could go back in time  and change one thing about the film it  would be that they would not have died  hemsworth's eyebrows blonde  while most viewers weren't bothered by  or even noticed  thor's light eyebrows others had a more  extreme reaction  feige further explained his feelings  about the dye job to uprocks  hemsworth was great and awesome and  pulled it off but there are a couple of  shots i watch  and i'm like oh my god that poor guy we  made him freaking dye his eyebrows  that's ridiculous  and i can laugh about it now because  hemsworth is thor  and he doesn't need long hair or a cape  or a hammer  or two eyeballs to beat thor when you're  making a movie  you have to make some tough decisions  nobody knows this  better than writer director james gunn  who's never been shy when it comes to  talking about personal favorite scenes  and lines  that didn't make the final cut of his  various directorial efforts  in terms of his first motion picture for  the marvel cinematic universe  he openly talked about how one of his  favorite lines and guardians of the  galaxy  was omitted from the film's final cut  the line in question is a follow-up to a  discussion that was used in the movie  in which peter quilt notes that he comes  from a planet of outlaws  drax responds that this sounds like a  place he'd like to explore  which inspires peter to casually say  that drax should come and visit sometime  in the final cut this is the end of  their exchange  however originally drax also noted that  while he was on earth he would like to  quote  kill many people there the brutal joke  ended up on the cutting room floor  but gunn loves the line so much that he  said the following on twitter i so  wanted george lucas it back in  i can't tell you that makes it pretty  apparent that this is one line  gunn regrets leaving behind from the  theatrical version of guardians of the  galaxy  while gunn might feel some  disappointment about this one missed  moment  drax still delivered some of our  favorite lines of the movie  you're an imbecile filmmaker louis  letterier  has had a career resurgence in recent  years thanks to his work directing  episodes of netflix tv shows like the  dark crystal age of resistance  and lupine however long before those  programs  leteriae helmed big budget blockbusters  like the second marvel cinematic  universe movie ever  the incredible hulk that feature ended  up becoming an odd duck  in the mcu pantheon thanks to a variety  of factors  including how the film's lead actor  edward norton never reprised the role  again  as well as its distribution rights  belonging to universal pictures  latier himself has contributed to the  weird reputation of the incredible hulk  by openly expressing his regrets about  shortcomings with the project  latier told huffpost back in 2013 i've  started movies without screenplays both  on clash of the titans and on hulk  and that is tremendously stressful  because you have a tendency to  overcompensate with effects  you haven't tested it in your head you  didn't run it over and over again and  figure it out he also noted that some  parts of the incredible hulk  are more identifiably his than others  laterier explained  the first half of the movie is really  mine and the second half is the studio's  expected hulk movie  two giants kicking each other's ass the  incredible hulk didn't quite  match people's expectations either  critically or financially  and it apparently didn't reach latier's  own ambitions either  phil coulson became such a beloved  character during his time in the marvel  cinematic universe that many fans  upon seeing him perish at loki's hand in  the avengers  wanted nothing more than for him to  return well they got their wish  and then some since coulson was brought  back for the abc  tv series agents of shield co-created by  avengers director  joss whedon the decision to resurrect  this character inspired as many fans as  it did to tractors with skeptics opining  that going down this route was a cheap  storytelling ploy  surprisingly whedon himself actually  fell  into the ladder camp in the spring of  2015  whedon told mental floss that bringing  back coulson removed quote  some of the punch out of his death scene  for me he then went on to say that the  whole  ordeal of reviving coulson reflected  some of his own  issues with blockbuster storytelling  during his mental floss  interview whedon elaborated on the topic  it's difficult because you're living in  a franchise world  you can't kill anyone or anybody  significant i think it's disingenuous to  say we're going to fight this great  battle but there's not going to be any  loss  so my feeling in these situations with  marvel is that if somebody has to be  placed on the altar and sacrificed  i'll let you guys decide if they stay  there while coulson returning may have  been a dream come true for some fans  for whedon it was a much more  complicated experience that brought in  moments of reflection  and regret still plenty of fans had  another reaction to coulson's  resurrection  in his second appearance in the marvel  cinematic universe  andy circus made a memorable splash as  ulysses claw  and in a rare live-action turn from the  actor in a blockbuster movie  circus proved he didn't need motion  capture to bring the goods to the big  screen  throughout a film that covered some very  heavy material  claw provided moments of welcome levity  during his reprisal of the hattaway song  what is love  and in his joy about sending a bevy of  cash flying in every direction during a  casino fight  claw proved such an enjoyable presence  in the film  in fact that even black panther writer  director ryan coogler  regrets killing off the character in the  middle of the movie a few months after  black panther hit theaters  coogler told the toronto sun i like claw  i was bugged by having to do that  it's tough when you have to kill  characters off and i really did love  that character  i love andy he's a lovely person but  again it's one of those things where  when you've got so many people in a  movie  some of them have to go it's  understandable that coogler would want  to keep claw around  given how positively the villain was  received however  at the very least couglar can take  solace in knowing that he wrote a  character who's so memorable  that people miss him when he's gone when  it came time for marvel to make a live  action feature film adaptation of doctor  strange there were several thorny  elements of the classic version of the  superhero that needed to be ironed out  chiefly the dr strange story originally  had a problematic approach to eastern  culture  that included the initial incarnation of  wong as  merely being a manservant another issue  concerned the character  of the ancient one a mentor who if  executed wrong  could have been seen as a wisened asian  master stereotype  marvel's decision on how to approach the  character of the ancient one  was to cast decidedly caucasian  performer tilda swinton  as the tibetan marvel comics character  according to dr  strange director scott derrickson the  reason they went with a white woman  instead of an asian actress was to avoid  the dragon lady stereotype  however the casting decision inspired a  wave of controversy and  accusations of whitewashing making  things even more complicated  dr strange screenwriter c robert cargill  also revealed that another reason for  the casting was to not offend  the chinese government which has a very  charged history with tibet  naturally this only inspired further  uproar  swinton's casting has become so infamous  that even mcu boss kevin feige has gone  on record to say  we thought we were being so smart and so  cutting edge  we are not going to do the cliche of the  wise and  old wise asian man but it was a wake-up  call to say  well wait a minute is there any other  way to figure it out is there any other  way to both  not fall into the cliche and cast an  asian actor  the answer to that of course is yes  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the marvel cinematic universe  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

